@startuml remote-worker-turn
title Remote worker turn (revision 4; B boundary shown, disabled until separate provisioner spec/qualification): the harness has no local tools; the relay (harness identity) forwards to the bridge service (bridge identity), which carries every tool call and the mailbox over ONE SSH connection from the donor to our host; our host never connects back

box "Donor machine: harness identity (sandboxed, egress = proxy only)" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "Harness\n(Claude / Codex / Muse, lockdown plan)" as H
  participant "swarma-remote-tools\n(stdio relay; no keys, no network)" as MCP
  participant "Provider proxy" as PX
end box
box "Donor machine: bridge identity (keys, audit, cursors)" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "Bridge service\n(supervisor + SSH client + signer + admission)" as SUP
end box
box "Our host" #WhiteSmoke
  participant "sshd + forced command\nswarma-rb-exec (workplace user)" as RB
  participant "Workplace\n(OS-user backend, swarma-workplace-exec/1)" as WP
  participant "Bridge\n(broker, mailbox, M3)" as BR
end box
participant "Orchestrator" as O

note over H, SUP
  The role split is enforced by UID/sandbox in B; sandbox only in C; A shares the donor UID,
  has no OS isolation/egress guarantee, and relies on qualified lockdown with no local tools.
  Relay has no keys/network in every variant; protocol/backend closed formats are pending.
end note

== standing connection ==
SUP -> RB: ssh workplace-user@host with K_ssh + short user-CA certificate;\nhost certificate checked on EVERY connection: pinned host CA, host name, validity, KRL (no TOFU)
note over SUP, RB: Bridge renews short user certificate; expiry/revocation refuses; retire stops renewal and closes sessions.
break failed host trust / expired or revoked user certificate / wrong workplace principal
  SUP -> SUP: refuse connection; no TOFU or alternate trust source
end
RB --> SUP: hello {versions:[1]} / swarma-rb/1 channel open (bounded CBOR frames, flow credits)
SUP -> RB: policy.get
RB --> SUP: workplace policy {tools, write scope, network, limits, env_allow} -> effective tool set
note right of RB: Match block: root-controlled TrustedUserCAKeys + KRL + workplace principal, no forwarding, no PTY,\nno user rc/env; forced command by absolute path; reconnect is the donor side's job

== launch ==
SUP -> SUP: obtain the composed plan from the construction site (agents-management);\ncheck expect_pin, tool_posture=lockdown, permissions=remote-auto, policy generation, qualified tuple;\nvalidate the expanded launch against the generated policy; resolve credential_binding/1
break unqualified/changed/unreadable executable, wrong pin/posture/permissions/generation or credential binding
  SUP -> SUP: refuse before exec; no alternate harness/source
end
SUP -> H: consume composed plan, launch exact qualified build;\nB: harness UID + sandbox + per-UID egress; C: donor UID + sandbox;\nA: donor UID, no OS confinement, direct provider path; credential per launch (CIP-0010)
H -> MCP: MCP initialize; tools/list = effective set (policy intersection)

== task arrives ==
O -> BR: signed task message to the worker (snapshot of one element)
BR -> BR: verify signature, grant, decision guard, fence; mailbox record; cursor++
BR -> RB: mailbox.notify {message_id, cursor} (advisory)
RB -> SUP: frame mailbox.notify
SUP -> RB: mailbox.read {from_cursor}
RB -> BR: read
BR --> RB: items + verification records
RB --> SUP: frames
SUP -> SUP: DONOR-SIDE ADMISSION: verification record present, target binding = this worker,\nunexpired, not fenced/revoked, delivery mode allowed; dedup by message_id; persist; cursor++
break absent/invalid verification, wrong binding, expired/fenced/revoked item or disallowed delivery mode
  SUP -> SUP: refuse input; do not apply a turn
end
SUP -> H: next turn through the session-input adapter: "validated message <id>" + snapshot
SUP -> RB: mailbox.applied {message_id} (application receipt, distinct from the transport reply)

== work ==
loop each tool call
  H -> MCP: tools/call bash {cmd, cwd, timeout}
  MCP -> SUP: forward over the relay socket (peer credentials checked)
  SUP -> SUP: audit line {tool, args_sha256, bytes, at}; budget counters (trusted side)
  break tool outside effective policy or wrong local peer
    SUP --> MCP: error result; audit refusal
    MCP --> H: unavailable tool
  end
  SUP -> RB: frame exec {id, op_key, cmd, cwd, env (env_allow only), timeout_s <= policy, max_output_bytes <= policy, lease_s}
  RB -> WP: run as the workplace user in its own process group with a lease; audit {who, what, when, policy id}
  WP --> RB: stdout/stderr frames (seq), exit
  RB --> SUP: frames (result cached by op_key for 10 min)
  SUP --> MCP: result
  MCP --> H: tool result
end
H -> PX: B/C: model API calls through the qualified proxy only
alt the model requests a built-in tool (Bash, Edit, WebFetch ...)
  H -> H: harness returns an error tool result (tool not available);\nthe tripwire logs the name after dispatch and may end the turn
end
alt SSH channel drops mid-turn
  SUP -> SUP: pause the turn loop; running turn continues to its deadline;\ntool calls fail with channel_down (retryable); result post queued durably with its op_key
  SUP -> RB: reconnect with backoff; host certificate/CA/validity/KRL rechecked; catch up from the durable cursor;\nreplay-safe: cached result or unknown_result, never a second effect
end

== result ==
H -> MCP: tools/call mailbox_post {binding, text} (offered only when the policy grants it)
MCP -> SUP: forward
SUP -> SUP: build the FINAL envelope (canonical bytes; audience/thread from the task record);\nsign with K_sig (D0 variant-specific storage; never sent to the project)
SUP -> RB: frame mailbox.post {op_key, envelope_bytes, signature}
RB -> BR: verify K_sig signature, grant, freshness; admit
BR -> O: carry the bytes UNCHANGED under the project bridge's carrier account for the worker (first slice) (distinct authority, audited) -> outcome proposal
note over H, O
  Phase: Draft donor target after slice 0; A first, B disabled, C qualified fallback.
  B proxy identity is bridge UID or a system service; A provider path is direct, no proxy.
  Bridge-role supervisor owns audit/budgets/cursors/dedup and durable queued results;
  harness role owns home/scratch; project bridge owns mailbox and project carrier credential;
  workplace executor owns job leases and op_key cache; root sshd owns CA/KRL/forced command.
  Exact service UIDs for project bridge, filenames and cache persistence format
  unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D5. rb/1 and workplace-exec/1 are pending design shorthand.
  [[../CIP-0008-remote-worker-launch-mode.md#recommendation CIP-0008 R3/R5/R9]]
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D0-D5/D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#tools-mailbox-and-lifecycle Delivery and reconnect]]
end note

@enduml
